# assets/profile.svg is generated by scripts/build_profile.py and is rewritten
# nightly by the Redraw workflow. Two sides editing it is normal, and a textual
# three-way merge on it is never correct — it produces a file with conflict
# markers inside the XML, which will not render.
#
# -merge makes git treat it as binary when merging: it reports the conflict and
# leaves the working tree copy intact instead of splicing the two versions.
# The resolution is always the same — rerun the build:
#
#     python scripts/build_profile.py
#
# -diff keeps generated art out of diffs, where it is noise.
assets/*.svg -merge -diff
